= Ingredients

@vegetable oil{3 3/4%tablespoons}\
@unsalted butter{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@butternut squash, peeled and cut into 1/2-inch pieces{1 7/8%pound}\
@large onion, chopped{1 1/4}\
@carrot, chopped{1 1/4}\
@celery rib, chopped{1 1/4}\
@garlic cloves, minced{2 1/2}\
@minced peeled ginger{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@curry powder (preferably Madras){1 1/4%tablespoon}\
@red lentils, picked over and rinsed{1 1/4%cup}\
@quarts water{2 1/2}\
@fresh lemon juice, or to taste{1 1/4%teaspoon}\
@chopped cilantro{5/8%cup}\
@vegetable oil{5/8%cup}\
@Accompaniment: cooked basmati rice{}

= Directions
Heat oil with butter in a large heavy pot over medium heat until foam subsides, then cook squash, onion, carrot, celery, garlic, ginger, and 1 teaspoon salt, stirring occasionally, until vegetables are softened and beginning to brown, 15 to 20 minutes.

Stir in curry powder and 1/4 teaspoon pepper and cook, stirring frequently, 2 minutes.

Add lentils and water and simmer, covered, until lentils are tender, 25 to 40 minutes. Stir in lemon juice and season with salt and pepper.

Purée cilantro, oil, and 1/2 teaspoon salt in a blender.

Serve soup drizzled with cilantro oil.
